WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.316
Once you've completed, send to Amazon Step 1, confirm inventory to send.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:10.000
You're ready for Step 2, confirm shipping.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.684
At the top of the page, you'll see your shipment method, which selects where you ship your products

00:00:15.684 --> 00:00:16.000
to.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.333
Amazon Fulfillment Center will be selected by default.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:26.000
If your shipment is eligible, you may see the option to select Amazon warehousing and distribution.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Selecting this option will take you to the Amazon warehousing and distribution AWD workflow.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.556
You can learn more about AWD by searching for Intro to Amazon warehousing and distribution in Seller

00:00:39.556 --> 00:00:40.000
University.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Next, you'll select your placement option.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.667
Start by choosing your shipping method between small parcel delivery, SPD, which are boxes that

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.000
are individually labeled,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:59.038
and less than and full truck load, LTL/FTL delivery, and whether you will be using an Amazon partnered

00:00:59.038 --> 00:01:02.000
carrier or a non-Amazon partnered carrier.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Using an Amazon partnered carrier offers discounted rates and in workflow label printing.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.600
If using a non-Amazon partnered carrier, you will be asked to provide a delivery window, which is

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:19.000
the calendar week when you expect your shipments to arrive at Amazon.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.000
You will then see the available shipment options and partnered carrier and placement costs.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:32.000
During busy periods, certain shipment options may be unavailable or listed with potential for delays.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
You may also see an option to adjust your delivery window or freight-ready date to reduce delays.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.478
You can adjust your selections to recalculate potential shipping costs and minimize delays until

00:01:43.478 --> 00:01:47.000
you find an option that best fits your business.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.000
However, it is essential that your delivery window or freight-ready date is accurate.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.893
Accurate dates allow us to properly manage inventory and reduce delays, and any information related

00:01:58.893 --> 00:02:04.000
to receive delays or options being unavailable are specific to the dates provided.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.684
Underneath the shipment options, you will see cards for each shipment you will be sending to a fulfillment

00:02:09.684 --> 00:02:10.000
center.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.714
In most cases, shipping plans will consist of up to five shipments.

00:02:14.714 --> 00:02:20.607
Each card is automatically updated with the selections you choose in the shipment options section

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.000
above.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.913
If you selected small parcel delivery with a non-Amazon partnered carrier, you will need to select

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.000
your carrier from the drop-down.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.310
The same carrier must be used for all small parcel shipments in a workflow.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:40.000
Note that any changes made to the shipment cards may impact the estimated total cost.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.667
Finally, review the estimated shipping and placement charges in the bottom right corner before accepting

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.000
and confirming shipping.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:59.000
You're now ready to move on to send to Amazon Step 3, Print Box Labels.
